  "info": {
    "description": "Point-in-time EPS consensus with per-estimate split adjustment: what the consensus was\n*as it could have been known* on a date, with every estimate's share basis resolved\nindividually around stock splits.\n\n**Data.** Analyst estimates are **synthetic** (seeded). EPS actuals (SEC EDGAR),\nearnings-release times and corporate actions (SEC filings and other primary sources) are\nreal.\n\n**Conventions.** A bare date means the end of that day, UTC. `basis=adjusted` puts every\nvalue on the latest share basis; `basis=unadjusted` shows what a screen showed that day.\nErrors are typed (`InvalidRequest` 400, `NotFound` 404).\n\n**Versioning.** The API is versioned by date; this is version `2026-10`.\n\n**One schema, four outputs.** This spec and the Python (Pydantic) and TypeScript (Zod)\nSDKs are generated from the same Pydantic models. The MCP tools validate their arguments\nwith those same request models and advertise the same formats. CI fails if any of them\ndrifts. Source and methodology: [github.com/LZL0/zacks-pit-demo](https://github.com/LZL0/zacks-pit-demo).\n",
    "title": "Point-in-time consensus demo",
    "version": "2026-10"
  },
  "openapi": "3.1.0",
  "paths": {
    "/consensus": {
      "get": {
        "description": "EPS consensus for one security and fiscal year exactly as it could have been\ncomputed at `as_of`: mean, median, high, low, stdev and count, every contributing\nestimate with its share-basis decision, every exclusion with its reason, and the\ncorporate actions applied. Fewer than 3 qualifying estimates returns 200 with\n`insufficient: true`.",
        "operationId": "get_consensus_consensus_get",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "in": "query",
            "name": "ticker",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "$ref": "#/components/schemas/TickerParam"
            }
          },
          {
            "in": "query",
            "name": "period",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "$ref": "#/components/schemas/PeriodParam"
            }
          },
          {
            "in": "query",
            "name": "as_of",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "$ref": "#/components/schemas/InstantParam"
            }
          },
          {
            "in": "query",
            "name": "basis",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "default": "adjusted",
              "enum": [
                "adjusted",
                "unadjusted"
              ],
              "title": "Basis",
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          {
            "description": "Ignore corporate actions announced after this instant.",
            "in": "query",
            "name": "known_as_of",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "anyOf": [
                {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/InstantParam"
                },
                {
                  "type": "null"
                }
              ],
              "description": "Ignore corporate actions announced after this instant.",
              "title": "Known As Of"
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ConsensusResult"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Successful Response"
          },
          "400": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "InvalidRequest: a parameter is malformed"
          },
          "404": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
